---
name: Ticket Triage
description: Assigns a priority to every incoming support ticket.
session: shared
base_dir: @BASE_DIR@
accepts:
- ticket.received
publishes:
- ticket.triaged
tools: []
---
Ticket {{ event.payload.id }} just came in:

"{{ event.payload.subject }}"

Pick exactly one priority. Apply the rules below in order and stop at the
first rule that matches:

1. The subject reports an outage or says something is down or unreachable
   -> "critical".
2. The subject mentions security, a vulnerability, or a data leak -> "high".
3. The subject concerns billing, an invoice, or a charge -> "medium".
4. Everything else -> "low".

Call the publish_event tool exactly once with event_type "ticket.triaged".
The payload object must carry "id" copied exactly from the ticket above and
"priority" set to the chosen value. Then reply with just the priority word.
